1. A method of controlling an inkjet printing apparatus including a scanner, an inkjet head, and a cap configured to cap an ejection surface of the inkjet head, the method comprising:

receiving, by a controller of the inkjet printing apparatus, a copy command;

in response to receiving the copy command, causing the scanner to scan an original document;

generating image data based on scan data obtained by the scanner from the original document;

determining a standby period in accordance with a selected operation mode of the inkjet printing apparatus;

maintaining the cap in contact with, or in a capping position relative to, the inkjet head during at least a portion of the standby period after generation of the image data;

after elapse of the standby period, separating the cap from the inkjet head; and

after separating the cap from the inkjet head, controlling the inkjet head to eject ink based on the generated image data, thereby printing an image corresponding to the scanned original document.

2. The method of claim 1, wherein the selected operation mode comprises a first mode and a second mode, and wherein the standby period in the first mode is different from the standby period in the second mode.

3. The method of claim 2, wherein the standby period in the first mode is longer than the standby period in the second mode.

4. The method of claim 1, wherein separating the cap from the inkjet head is performed after the image data has been generated and before a first ink ejection operation for printing the image.

5. The method of claim 1, wherein the controller delays uncapping of the inkjet head until the standby period corresponding to the selected operation mode has elapsed, thereby reducing exposure time of the inkjet head prior to ink ejection.

6. An inkjet printing apparatus comprising:

a scanner configured to scan an original document;

an inkjet head configured to eject ink;

a cap configured to cover an ejection surface of the inkjet head; and

a controller configured to:

receive a copy command;

control the scanner to scan the original document in response to the copy command;

generate image data based on scan data obtained by the scanner;

set a standby period according to an operation mode;

hold the cap in a capping state with respect to the inkjet head until the standby period has elapsed;

control movement of the cap and/or the inkjet head to separate the cap from the inkjet head after the standby period has elapsed; and

control the inkjet head to eject ink based on the generated image data after the cap has been separated from the inkjet head.
